{
 "encounter_id": "00800",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Mr Gallagher? I'm Una, I'll check you first. You're looking flushed. Arm out. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I feel rotten. Cold. Aching. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Temperature 37.9, pulse 104, blood pressure 108 over 66, oxygen 97 percent.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mr Gallagher, I'm Dr Moran. Una says you're unwell with a cold and you take adrenal tablets. Tell me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've got Addison's. Hydrocortisone. I've a cold since Monday. Aching, sore throat, snotty. And I feel weak."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Weak how?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Legs heavy. Dizzy when I stand."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any vomiting or diarrhoea?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Not yet."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you doubled your hydrocortisone, the sick day rule? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I took my usual. Didn't think. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's the reason you're feeling so rough, probably. Any abdominal pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any confusion, or have you passed out?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Appendix, in 1999."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Who do you live with, who'd notice if you got worse?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My brother."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me examine you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your throat's red, your chest is clear, and your skin is warm and dry, but you're a little dehydrated."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "His blood pressure's low for him, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Noted. Mr Gallagher, with Addison's, a cold can tip you into a crisis if your steroid dose isn't increased. So I'd say this is early adrenal insufficiency brought on by the infection, but I can't rule out a crisis."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A crisis? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A dangerous drop in your steroid level. We'll prevent it. I'd like you to take hydrocortisone 20 mg now, and then 20 mg twice a day for three days."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll get his first dose now, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd also like you to take paracetamol, 1 gram, for the fever and aches, up to four times a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to take blood tests for salts, sugar and infection, and I'd like him to wait here for an hour, until the BP improves."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll set him up in the bay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Drink plenty of fluids, salty ones if you can."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you vomit, can't keep your tablets down, or get very drowsy, you need an injection, and the ambulance, straight away. Tell your brother."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. I carry the injection kit. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. ~"
  }
 ],
